/*  `cufet` blocks and `Cite` — `src/Interpreter/CiteExpansion.cs`.

    ★ A block that says nothing about what it gives back is SOURCE, held until a `Cite` places it:
    each `Cite <name>.` is replaced by what the block holds, before anything is gathered, so a cited
    object is an ordinary type of the program and a cited `Define` an ordinary local where it lands.
    The blocks stay in the program, and the only thing still asked of one is that `cufet` is pulled.

    ⚠ What a block holds may reach only for what belongs to the program — a free function, a type,
    a `permanently` constant, a pulled book — since anything else would mean whatever the citing
    site happens to have under that name.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// The program with every `Cite` replaced by what its block holds — or the refusal.
    Bind node or failure to expand-cites unto checker, given (the node program):
        Define blocks as a map from text to node.
        Define block-order as a series of text.
        Define runnable as a map from text to fact.
        Define cited as a series of node.
        Cast gather-citing on (program, blocks, block-order, runnable, cited) or pass the failure off.
        If the number of block-order is 0 and the number of cited is 0, return program.

        Define scope-names as cast program-scope-names on (program).
        For each block-name in block-order, repeat:
            Define block as the entry for block-name in blocks but void is cast unknown-type.
            Cast require-declarations-only on (block) or pass the failure off.
            Cast require-no-capture on (block, scope-names) or pass the failure off.
        Done.

        // A block holding a function may only be cited where functions belong.
        Define places-function as a map from text to fact.
        For each block-name in block-order, repeat:
            Define block as the entry for block-name in blocks but void is cast unknown-type.
            For each held in (cast field-of on (block, 2))'s children, repeat:
                If held's kind is "BindStatement", in places-function, the entry for block-name becomes true.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define function-scope as a map from text to fact.
        For each statement in cast hoistable on (program), repeat:
            If statement's kind is "CiteStatement", in function-scope, the entry for cast cite-key on (statement) becomes true.
        Done.
        Return cast placed-cites on (program, blocks, runnable, places-function, function-scope) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    Bind text to cite-key, given (the node citation):
        Return "{(cast field-of on (citation, 2))'s word}:{(cast field-of on (citation, 3))'s word}".
    Done.

    /// Every block, runnable cufet axiom and `Cite`, in the order they are written — not looking
    /// inside a block, whose contents are not in the program until something cites them.
    Bind void or failure to gather-citing, given (the node tree, the map from text to node blocks, the series of text block-order,
            the map from text to fact runnable, the series of node cited):
        Define kind as tree's kind.
        If kind is "atom", return.
        If kind is "CufetAxiomDefinition":
            Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tree, 1)).
            Define first as the entry for name in blocks.
            If first is not void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("there is already cufet source called '{name}', on line {(cast field-of on (first, 3))'s word}",
                    "A name holds one block, because a 'Cite' of it has to say which one without looking anywhere else",
                    cast numeric on (cast field-of on (tree, 3)), "declare a second block called '{name}'",
                    "Give this one another name, or fold the two together.")).
            Done.
            In blocks, the entry for name becomes tree.
            Insert name into block-order.
            Return.
        Done.
        If kind is "BindStatement" and (cast bind-mark on (tree, ":FromAxiomLanguage") in lowercase) is "cufet":
            In runnable, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tree, 1)) becomes true.
        Done.
        If kind is "CiteStatement", insert tree into cited.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Cast gather-citing on (child, blocks, block-order, runnable, cited) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `ProgramScopeNames`: free functions, `permanently` constants and pulled books where hoisting
    /// reaches, and every type anywhere outside a block.
    Bind map from text to fact to program-scope-names, given (the node program):
        Define names as a map from text to fact.
        For each statement in cast hoistable on (program), repeat:
            If statement's kind is "BindStatement" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)):
                In names, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) becomes true.
            Done.
            If statement's kind is "DefineStatement" and cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)):
                In names, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) becomes true.
            Done.
            If statement's kind is "PullStatement":
                For each pulled in (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children, repeat:
                    For each part in pulled's children, repeat:
                        In names, the entry for cast unquoted on (part) becomes true.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Cast gather-type-names on (program, names).
        Return names.
    Done.

    Bind void to gather-type-names, given (the node tree, the map from text to fact names):
        Define kind as tree's kind.
        If kind is "atom" or kind is "CufetAxiomDefinition", return.
        If kind is "ObjectDefinition" or kind is "InterfaceDefinition":
            In names, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tree, 1)) becomes true.
        Done.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Cast gather-type-names on (child, names).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// Where a statement inside a block is said to be — its own line, or the block's when it has
    /// none. ⚠ C# finds it by reflection; the kinds not listed are left unjudged rather than guessed.
    Bind number or failure to held-row, given (the node statement, the number block-row):
        Define place as 0.
        Judge statement's kind, where it is:
            It is "StateStatement" or "IfStatement" or "StopStatement" or "SkipStatement" or "RepeatUntilStatement", return block-row.
            It is "ReturnStatement" or "ExitStatement", the place becomes 2.
            It is "CastStatement" or "BecomesStatement" or "PullStatement" or "PullRabbitStatement" or "CiteStatement" or "WhileStatement", the place becomes 3.
            It is "ForEachStatement", the place becomes 4.
            Otherwise, return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a cufet block holding a {statement's kind}")).
        Done.
        Return cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, place)).
    Done.

    /// `RequireDeclarationsOnly`: source takes no parameters, and holds only declarations.
    Bind void or failure to require-declarations-only, given (the node block):
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (block, 1)).
        Define block-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (block, 3)).
        If cast bind-mark on (block, ":HasParameterClause") is "true":
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                "'{name}' says nothing about what it gives back, so it is source rather than something to run — and source takes no parameters",
                "A parameter's value comes from a call, and nothing calls this: it is placed where a 'Cite' says",
                block-row, "give '{name}' parameters",
                "Drop the 'given' clause — or say what running it gives back, as in 'Define cufet number {name}, given (…), as [ … ].'")).
        Done.
        For each statement in (cast field-of on (block, 2))'s children, repeat:
            Define kind as statement's kind.
            If kind is not "ObjectDefinition" and kind is not "InterfaceDefinition" and kind is not "DefineStatement" and kind is not "BindStatement":
                Define at-row as cast held-row on (statement, block-row) or pass the failure off.
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("cufet source holds declarations, and this is not one",
                    "A cited block places what it declares where the 'Cite' is. An object, an interface and a 'Define' are what it can declare so far",
                    at-row, "put this inside '{name}'",
                    "Move it out of the block, or declare an object or an interface here.")).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `RequireNoCapture`: a `Define`'s value in a block reads only what the block declares, what
    /// belongs to the program, and the pronouns.
    Bind void or failure to require-no-capture, given (the node block, the map from text to fact scope-names):
        Define visible as a map from text to fact.
        For each mapping in scope-names, repeat:
            In visible, the entry for the key of mapping becomes true.
        Done.
        For each statement in (cast field-of on (block, 2))'s children, repeat:
            Define kind as statement's kind.
            If kind is "DefineStatement" or kind is "ObjectDefinition" or kind is "InterfaceDefinition":
                In visible, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) becomes true.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each pronoun in a series with ("it", "one", "input", "failure", "the failure"), repeat:
            In visible, the entry for pronoun becomes true.
        Done.
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (block, 1)).
        For each statement in (cast field-of on (block, 2))'s children, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "DefineStatement":
                Cast refuse-capture on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), visible, name) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to refuse-capture, given (the node tree, the map from text to fact visible, the text block-name):
        Define kind as tree's kind.
        If kind is "atom", return.
        If kind is "VariableReference":
            Define read as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tree, 1)).
            If (the entry for read in visible) is not void, return.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                "cufet source cannot reach for '{read}' — it declares no such name, and one it does not declare would mean whatever the site that cites it happens to have",
                "A block may use what belongs to the program — a function, a type, a 'permanently' constant, a pulled book — because those mean the same thing wherever it is placed",
                cast numeric on (cast field-of on (tree, 2)), "read '{read}' inside '{block-name}'",
                "Declare '{read}' inside the block, or make it a 'permanently' constant outside it.")).
        Done.
        If kind is "LambdaLiteral":
            Define inner as a map from text to fact.
            For each mapping in visible, repeat:
                In inner, the entry for the key of mapping becomes true.
            Done.
            For each parameter-name in cast bound-names-of on (cast field-of on (tree, 1)), repeat:
                In inner, the entry for parameter-name becomes true.
            Done.
            Cast refuse-capture on (cast field-of on (tree, 2), inner, block-name) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Cast refuse-capture on (child, visible, block-name) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The tree with each `Cite` replaced by what its block holds.
    Bind node or failure to placed-cites, given (the node tree, the map from text to node blocks, the map from text to fact runnable,
            the map from text to fact places-function, the map from text to fact function-scope):
        If tree's kind is "atom", return tree.
        Define rebuilt as a new node { the kind tree's kind, the word tree's word, the children a series of node }.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            If child's kind is "CiteStatement" and tree's kind is "list":
                Define spliced as cast held-by-cite on (child, blocks, runnable, places-function, function-scope) or pass the failure off.
                For each held in spliced's children, repeat:
                    Cast rebuilt's add on (held).
                Done.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Cast rebuilt's add on (cast placed-cites on (child, blocks, runnable, places-function, function-scope) or pass the failure off).
            Done.
        Done.
        Return rebuilt.
    Done.

    /// What one `Cite` places — or why it cannot.
    Bind node or failure to held-by-cite, given (the node citation, the map from text to node blocks, the map from text to fact runnable,
            the map from text to fact places-function, the map from text to fact function-scope):
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (citation, 1)).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (citation, 2)).
        Define block as the entry for name in blocks.
        If block is not void:
            If (the entry for name in places-function) is not void and (the entry for cast cite-key on (citation) in function-scope) is void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' holds a function, so it cannot be cited inside another body",
                    "Placed here it would be a closure over the body citing it, and what a block holds must mean the same thing wherever it is placed. Placed where functions belong it is a free function, which already cannot read the data around it",
                    at-row, "cite '{name}' inside a body",
                    "Cite '{name}' at the top level, or directly inside a 'Pull' block.")).
            Done.
            Return cast field-of on (block, 2).
        Done.
        If (the entry for name in runnable) is not void:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' says what it gives back, so it is something you run rather than source to cite",
                "A cufet axiom that names a result is a body with a name — the same rule the c-language tag follows",
                at-row, "cite '{name}'",
                "Call it: 'cast {name} on (...)'. Only a block that says nothing about a result is cited.")).
        Done.
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("there is no cufet source called '{name}' to cite",
            "'Cite' places what a cufet block holds, and the name is the block's, not a variable's",
            at-row, "cite '{name}'",
            "Declare it first: 'Define cufet {name} as [ ... ].'")).
    Done.
Done.
